there always seems to be room for a few  more bad guys in the marvel cinematic  universe and if the mcu is going to  introduce a few more villains next time  around  here's how they could expand to include  some of their best and weirdest comics  bad guys in avengers 4.  one of the most interesting aspects of  infinity war is that thanos's infamous  snap of the fingers straight up killed  people rather than erasing them from  existence  that means there are a lot of  superheroes in that world who are dead  and since it stands to reason that at  least a few of them will make it back to  the land of the living  that means that they've got to be  somewhere else in the meantime  that opens up the possibility of  introducing mephisto the marvel  universe's most prominent take on the  devil  there are even connections that are  already waiting to be explored  mephisto's role as a bargainer means  that he could be in a perfect position  to trade something for the heroes lives  we know from dr strange that tony stark  staying alive is necessary for the  heroes to win  so maybe there's something tony has that  mephisto wants  maybe captain america is going to strike  a deal to bring back his two best  friends  or considering that mephisto was the one  who drove nakia to become a supervillain  in the comics by exploiting her love her  t'challa  maybe she'll be the one who has to make  a sacrifice to bring the black panther  back from the dead  there's another fun piece of the finger  snap it's not just earth that's affected  it's explicitly mentioned several times  that thanos is killing half the universe  which means that all of those  space-faring societies that we've seen  in the guardians of the galaxy movies  have also been hit  that leaves outer space weakened and  destabilized on a cosmic scale  making it the perfect time for a galaxy  conquering super villain to show up and  start destroying things  and there's no one better for that role  than a nihilus in the comics he's  essentially a sentient space locust hell  bent on devouring  everything in his path across the galaxy  since thanos has apparently retired to a  farm at the end of infinity war  temporarily shifting the focus to a more  vicious thread could be a good way to  show how big the stakes have gotten  half the universe dying is bad but it's  better than the other half being wiped  out by a dude who calls himself the  living death  if the mcu is looking to introduce a  villain that could rival thanos  then they might decide to go with one of  the greats dr doom  decades of stories where he fights iron  man doctor strange and even spider-man  have shown us that he's adaptable and  powerful enough to pose a threat to  anyone  including thanos himself he's even one  of the few villains to team up with the  heroes in the original infinity gauntlet  story and has had designs on the stones  more than a few times in the years since  of course there's an obvious sticking  point here despite his career of  fighting the whole marvel universe  doom will always be the arch nemesis of  the fantastic four  and the film rights to those characters  were held by fox  with the news that disney was buying out  fox and getting those rights back  however the ff could eventually find a  home in the mcu  it's pretty much inevitable although  kevin feige has said that there are only  vague ideas about how to bring those  characters into the mcu  and that the next few movies including  avengers 4 were set in stone well before  the buyout  while it's tempting to focus solely on  massive cosmic threats  there's plenty of room for more minor  villains to step into the spotlight  and take advantage of the chaos that  results from half the population of a  planet turning to dust  believe it or not that makes avengers 4  the perfect opportunity to introduce the  jackal  best known as the villain directly  responsible for the infamous clone saga  peter parker is one of the characters  who gets dusted by thanos  meaning that there's currently no place  for one of marvel's flagship characters  in the next film  there are ways around that of course  homecoming already hinted at the  existence of miles morales  but they could always decide that a  clone of peter is a good way to go  if that seems unlikely consider this in  the comics the jackal is miles warren  who was one of peter's college  professors before he got obsessed with  cloning spider-man and gwen stacy  she's never named in the film but if you  look at the credits for homecoming  you'll find that orange is the new  blacks salinas leyva plays a teacher  named miss warren  maybe it's a coincidence over the mcu  you never know  one of the more unexpected moments of  infinity war involved a reappearance  from the red skull as a cosmic harbinger  of doom  since he's captain america's  arch-nemesis it makes sense that he  would somehow find his way back into  action  but now it seems that brock rumlow aka  crossbones is going to be back in  avengers 4 in some way too  at this point that could mean anything  from a flashback sequence to a scene in  the afterlife  but it could also mean that we'll be  seeing characters returning from the  dead who weren't just snapped into dust  if that's the case then why stop at  skull and bones why not go  all out with the whole dang skeleton  crew admittedly mother knight and  minister blood aren't exactly going to  set the world on fire  but they're no more or less well-known  than proxima midnight and corvus glaive  so hey why not finally we have the  character who's quite possibly the most  marvel comics of all the marvel villains  modoc  the mental organism designed only for  killing the mcu has gotten weird enough  that we've seen etre the dwarf  the grand master and a cameo appearance  from beta ray bill  arnhem zola has been in two movies and  while he admittedly never appeared in  his true comic book form as a big robot  dude with a tv  face in his chest winter soldier brought  him pretty close  so why not follow up the biggest and  most devastating superhero movie of all  time by throwing in the mental organism  designed only for killing  he's not the giant head in a flying  rocket chair that we want  he's the giant head in a flying rocket  chair that we need
 

